# NVIDIA ModelOpt mixed-precision checkpoint of Qwen3.8-27B (nvidia/Qwen3.8-27B-NVFP4, rev 482ca0f3).
# NVFP4 on the MLP layers + lm_head, FP8 on attention / linear-attention, native MTP layer kept.
# ~21.9 GB. Same architecture, 256K context and vision as qwen3.8-27b (BF16). On GB10 the FP4
# layers run as W4A16 (no native FP4 tensor-core path), but the ~60% smaller weights cut the
# bandwidth-bound decode cost.
#
# DEFAULT since 2026-11-10. VALIDATED on vLLM v0.33.0-aarch64: swap-ui stability battery passed
# (30/30 serving, 54.5 tok/s aggregate at concurrency 4). MTP sweep, same harness and tests as the
# BF16 qwen3.8-27b (ai-tools gpu/docs/vllm-0.33-quant-comparison-2026-11.md).
# Single / conc-4 tok/s, 32-trial tool gate, MMLU 10/subtask n=570:
#     no spec        12.51 / 46.46   0/32   MMLU 0.851 +/- 0.015   KV 1.85M tok
#     k=3            28.59 / 97.39   0/32                          KV 1.59M
#     k=4            27.68 / 94.79   0/32                          KV 1.56M
#     k=5 (landed)   28.55 / 91.91   0/32   MMLU 0.851 +/- 0.015   KV 1.54M   <- the recipe setting
#     k=5 + bf16 KV  27.04 / 100.94  0/32   MMLU 0.837 +/- 0.015   KV 0.84M   (not adopted)
#   vs BF16 qwen3.8-27b at k=5: 2.6x single, 2.2x conc-4, 2.7x KV capacity, MMLU 0.851 vs 0.856
#   (no measurable loss), load ~4 min vs ~9 (fastsafetensors).
#   MTP output drift vs no-spec is larger than on BF16 (greedy agreement 0.24-0.36 vs 0.885,
#   prompt-scoring mean |dlogprob| 0.22 vs 0.02). It is the same for k=3/4/5 and with bf16 KV, so
#   it is neither draft depth nor the FP8 KV cache. MMLU and the tool gate are unaffected.
#
# Settings follow the official vLLM recipe (vllm-project/recipes models/Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B.yaml,
# variant nvfp4_nvidia, hardware_overrides.dgx_spark_gb10; added in recipes#826 on 2026-09-15 by
# NVIDIA "in our testing"):
#   --kv-cache-dtype fp8, GPU util 0.7, max-model-len 262144, --max-num-seqs 8,
#   --max-num-batched-tokens 8192, --enable-chunked-prefill, --async-scheduling,
#   --enable-prefix-caching (gb10-serve.sh always adds it), --load-format fastsafetensors
#   (present in the v0.33.0 image). MTP k=5 is the recipe's dgx_spark_gb10 spec-decode override.
#   Tool parser qwen3_coder.
# VERSION MISMATCH: #826 names no vLLM build. Its review mentions nightly builds of the time
# (~Sept 2026, v0.30-era), and the recipe's other GB10 tool-call testing (recipes#1086) ran on the
# vllm/vllm-openai:qwen38 dev build (0.1.dev19754) with the Rust frontend. Neither is our v0.33.0
# release or our Python frontend, so these settings are "documented, unverified on our version"
# until the tests pass here.
# FP8 KV note: this checkpoint ships NO KV-cache scales (kv_cache_quant_algo: null), so fp8 KV
# uses default scales. Measured on v0.33.0 it costs nothing against bf16 KV: MMLU 0.851 vs 0.837,
# same drift, and it holds ~1.8x the KV tokens. Kept per the recipe.

# --- UI metadata ---
UI_LABEL="Qwen3.8-27B-NVFP4"
UI_DESC="Default. NVIDIA ModelOpt NVFP4/FP8 mixed checkpoint of Qwen3.8-27B with native MTP (k=5) and FP8 KV cache, per the vLLM GB10 recipe. ~21.9 GB, native 256K context, vision. Validated on vLLM v0.33.0: MMLU 0.851 (= BF16), tool gate 0/32, ~2.6x BF16 speed, 1.5M-token KV cache."
UI_SIZE="~21.9 GB · NVFP4/FP8 mixed · vision · 256K ctx"
UI_SPEED="~28.5 tok/s single, ~92 tok/s conc-4 (MTP k=5, measured 2026-11-10)"
UI_USE_CASES="Vision Q&A, Long-context (256K) reading, Agentic tool-use"
EXPERIMENTAL="0"

# --- Serve recipe ---
SERVE_MODEL="nvidia/Qwen3.8-27B-NVFP4"
SERVED_NAME="qwen3.8-27b-nvfp4"
SERVE_CONTAINER="swap-vllm-qwen3.8-27b-nvfp4"
SERVE_PORT="8002"
MAX_LEN="262144"
GPU_UTIL="0.7"
QUANT="auto"
TOOLS="1"
REASONING_PARSER="qwen3"
TOOL_PARSER="qwen3_coder"
KV_ARG="--kv-cache-dtype fp8"
GENCFG_ARG=""
EXTRA_ARGS="--max-num-seqs 8 --max-num-batched-tokens 8192 --enable-chunked-prefill --async-scheduling --load-format fastsafetensors"
SPEC_ARG="--speculative-config '{\"method\":\"mtp\",\"num_speculative_tokens\":5}'"
COMPILE_ARG=""
# The earlier NVFP4 init took ~930s, past the 900s default health wait (swapper #33).
SERVE_TIMEOUT="1500"
